# Every text file is stored as LF and checked out as LF, whatever core.autocrlf a
# contributor happens to have. Commits ebe79e1 and 37b391b flip-flopped
# scripts/run_campaign.py between CRLF and LF, turning a 16-line and a 2-line
# change into 6,300-line diffs; pinning the attribute here means that cannot recur.
#
# This does not rewrite anything that is already committed: text=auto leaves a blob
# that already contains CRLF alone until someone explicitly renormalizes it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Packaged release artifacts: eol conversion would corrupt the gzip streams, the
# fixed-size split parts that data/release/reassemble.sh concatenates, and the
# pickled value model. A textual diff of a several-hundred-MB corpus is unreadable
# anyway, so the dataset shards opt out of diffing too.
*.gz    binary
*.tgz   binary
*.tar   binary
*.part* binary
*.pkl   binary
*.jsonl -text -diff
